{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 101, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a residual skip gains far more than replacing an existing conv or pool there (exps 11,12,16-18 vs 13-15)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node1 has no direct path to the output, the skip edge restores connectivity and gives much larger gains (exps 17,18)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the residual skip with a conv removes the identity path and hurts, while filling an empty e3 helps strongly (exps 73,74 vs 71,72,76)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With e5 absent, e4 is a critical output path, so adding a conv there yields huge gains (exps 36,37)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing e5 when e4 is already none leaves the output with few or no paths, causing large drops (exps 54,55)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the e3 skip, the conv path through e5 matters more, so deleting it hurts more (exps 52,55,57,59 vs 51,56,58)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv to a cell otherwise built from weak 1x1 convs adds missing receptive field (exps 27-29 vs 21-26)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free skip on the final edge with conv3x3 yields bigger gains than replacing none or avg_pool (exps 8,9 vs 1-7)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a pool where there was nothing is mildly positive, whereas swapping a conv for a pool loses capacity (exps 94,96 vs 91,93,95,100)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the node1-to-output skip removes a residual path, which helps less or hurts compared with filling an empty e4 (exps 34,40 vs 31,36-38)."}], "tok": 32827, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_